Corrected vmalloc backport host regression models
================================================

From the repository root:

  python3 tools/testing/selftests/vmalloc_backport/test_backport.py --cc clang
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/vmalloc_backport/test_backport.py \
    --cc 'clang -fsanitize=undefined -fno-sanitize-recover=all'

Requires Python 3 and a GNU-C-compatible host compiler. HOSTCC is supported;
the default is cc. --source-root PATH selects another kernel source tree.
Build products use a temporary directory and are removed automatically.
No root access or running-kernel changes are needed. model.c is a template,
not a standalone kernel selftest executable. These standalone tests are not
added to the legacy top-level kselftest target list.

The runner extracts the production vmap layout, allocator and proc iterator,
seq-list helpers, list code, red-black tree and augmentation implementation.
It does not maintain a second copy of the allocator. Assertions are enabled
even when NDEBUG is supplied. Locks, slab, CPUs, atomics, pending lists, TLB
flushes and seq output have single-threaded mocks.

Coverage:
* 400,000 search/alignment/overflow comparisons against independent page-bitmap
  and 128-bit arithmetic oracles, plus the exact aligned-hole regression.
* 30,016 allocation/free/split/merge/GFP/failure operations; red-black tree,
  augmentation, ordering and page-coverage invariants.
* 4,014 congruent per-CPU allocation/oracle/rollback cases, with shuffled offset
  arrays and allocation-failure injection.
* Boot import success and all five occupied/free metadata allocation failures.
* Lazy quarantine until TLB flush, pending proc records with an empty busy
  tree or final vm_map_ram area, ordinary busy records, and iterator lock
  balance for complete reads, short reads, restarts, nonzero positions and EOF.
* Source guards for user-map alignment/flags, vendor interfaces, metadata
  ownership, GFP masking and intentional omission of donor #17.

Negative controls (each command MUST compile, then fail a C assertion):

  python3 tools/testing/selftests/vmalloc_backport/test_backport.py --cc clang --negative donor-search
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/vmalloc_backport/test_backport.py --cc clang --negative missing-unlock
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/vmalloc_backport/test_backport.py --cc clang --negative boot-skip
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/vmalloc_backport/test_backport.py --cc clang --negative wrong-gfp
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/vmalloc_backport/test_backport.py --cc clang --negative early-reuse

A compile failure or integration-guard failure is NOT a successful negative
control. Inspect the assertion diagnostic. Negative source changes affect
only the temporary extracted model, never the checkout.

These tests do not prove SMP memory ordering, real preemption/CPU hotplug,
lockdep correctness, hardware TLB behavior, vmalloc pressure/concurrency or
performance. See Documentation/vm/vmalloc-backport.rst for provenance,
intentional corrections, ARM64 object-build coverage and device follow-up.
